--- !u!114 &1000593
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1000149}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b220d359e73d41bcaad23ba68250ce11, type: 3}
  m_Name:
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  interactionPrompt: {fileID: 1000594}
  stationId: WX-04
  stationName: Weather Tower
  entries:
  - id: "004"
    title: "First Shift at WX-04"
    timestamp: "Day 12 · 07:40"
    body: "The west door stuck halfway open on my first shift. I cleared a washer from the bottom track and tried the door again. It closes cleanly now. I left the washer on the log desk in case it came from the hinge.\n\nUpstairs, the communications terminal was still showing yesterday’s outgoing message. I left it in the queue and wrote down the time. If it’s still there on the next shift, check the cable behind the service bench before restarting the terminal.\n\nThere’s a paper station map in the drawer beneath this computer. Someone drew the east lift on it by hand. Leave that copy in the tower so the next person can find it."
  - id: "003"
    title: "East Lift Stalled"
    timestamp: "Day 11 · 18:25"
    body: "The east lift stopped just below the upper landing while I was bringing up an empty crate. I sent it back down and tried again without the crate. It stopped at the same spot.\n\nI found a loose panel beside the upper guide rail and fastened it again. The lift reached both landings on the next trip. I left the crate downstairs until someone can test the lift with a load."
  - id: "002"
    title: "Power Lost Overnight"
    timestamp: "Day 11 · 02:13"
    body: "The lights went out during the overnight shift. The emergency strip by the west door stayed on, so I could reach the service bench without crossing the lift platform in the dark.\n\nPower came back after I swapped the supply connector with a spare. The log computer recovered the previous entry, but the communications terminal upstairs still needs a restart.\n\nThe connector I removed is in the shallow tray on the service bench. Please keep it there until the next maintenance visit."
  - id: "001"
    title: "Shift Handover"
    timestamp: "Day 10 · 20:10"
    body: "I moved the spare parts out of the doorway and put the unopened crates in the cargo hold. The open one by the repair station is waiting for inventory.\n\nI finished the walkthrough by the west entrance and left the main lift parked at ground level. The next shift can pick up the tool count from the sheet on the wall table."
